{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[A]Way down in Dixie, oh do they miss me
[D]Down along the Dixie [A]line
[A]Banjoes are strummin’, horseflies are hummin’
[B7]Ripe melons on the [D]vine
[F#m]The gold and [A]the gray [D]weeds sing [B7]look away
[A]Way down along [E]the Dixie [A]line
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I spent my childhood walking the wildwood
Down along the Dixie line
Freight trains are squallin’, eyeballs are ballin’
Four engines at a time
I was so happy with Momma and Pappy
Down along the Dixie line
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[A]Can't you hear those drivers [D]wail
Can't you [A]see those bright rails [E]shine
Gonna [A]catch that fireball [D]man
Leave the [F#m]northland [E]far [A]behind
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
A river of whiskey flows down in Dixie
Down along the Dixie line
They pulled up the tracks now, I can't go back now
Can't hardly keep from crying
Oh do they miss me way down in Dixie
Down along the Dixie line
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
Can't you hear those drivers wail
Can't you see those bright rails shine
Wanna catch that fireball man
Leave the northland far behind…
SOLO and REPEAT CHORUS x3
{end_of_verse}
